   "source": [
    "# Quiz: A Brief Introduction to Statistics and Probability\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-04-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Why statistics and probability are important for data science?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Because you cannot operate on data without knowing math</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You can work with data without deep math knowledge, though knowing the basics is better.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Because data science is a science and has strong formal foundation</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Statistics and probability are math areas that are highly relevant to data science. They help you prove ideas about data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Because we want to keep uneducated people from doing data science</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Statistics is not there to keep people out. You can work with data even without deep math knowledge.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-04-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Can you get heads 10 times in a row when throwing a coin?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>yes</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>no</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-04-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>When you throw a dice, what is the probability of getting an even number?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>1/2</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Three of the six outcomes are even, so the probability is 3/6, or 1/2.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>1/3</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Three of the six outcomes are even, so the probability is 3/6, or 1/2.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>impossible to tell</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You can work it out: three of the six outcomes are even, so it is 3/6, or 1/2.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-04-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>We want to prove that basketball players are taller than average people. We have collected heights of 20 people from both groups. What do we need to do?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>compare means</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A gap between two means could just be a statistical error. You need a formal test.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>collect more data, 20 is not enough!</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. What you need is a formal test, like the t-test, to check if the difference is real.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>use t-test</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A t-test checks whether the difference between two means is real or just a statistical error.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-04-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>How can we demonstrate that income of a person is dependent on the level of education?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>compute correlation coefficient</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A correlation coefficient shows how closely two values change together. A strong correlation is a good sign that they are connected.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>divide into educated and non-educated cohorts and compute means</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A gap between two group means can be just a statistical error. Correlation shows how two values change together.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>use t-test</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A t-test checks whether two groups differ. To see how two values change together, use correlation.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-04-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>We throw the dice 100 times and compute the average value. What would be the distribution of the result?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>uniform</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. One throw follows a uniform distribution, but the average of many throws follows a normal distribution.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>normal</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. By the central limit theorem, the average of many random values is normally distributed.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>none of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The central limit theorem says the average of many random values is normally distributed.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
